From 0b31e0e2421e3c37a42856eb26568fe6a54338cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grzegorz <grzegorz2047@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:22:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] xcl run: --in-process runs the host in the launcher's
 process

Wine on the PS5 (prospero-win) runs one process per program: the child
host process `xcl run` starts with CreateProcessW would not run there,
and its profiles cannot set XCL_HOST either (only DXVK_/VKD3D_/... names).

`xcl run --in-process <game> [-- args]` writes boot.json as before, then
sets the game folder as the current directory and calls host_main() in
this process. The title gets the command line the child would have had:
kernelx answers GetCommandLineW / GetCommandLineA (kernel32 imports are
routed there) with it, and the UCRT's cached _wcmdln / _acmdln, which a
dynamic-CRT title builds argv from, point at it. Without the flag
nothing changes: GetCommandLineW / A pass through to Windows.

Test: e2e test_title_runs_in_the_launchers_process runs the test title
with --in-process; its argv check fails without the command line
(argv[0] = ...\xcl.exe), measured by disabling set_command_line().

Measured on an RTX 3060 Laptop GPU, Windows 11, Rust 1.100 debug:
cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast -- --test-threads=4: 976 passed,
1 failed, 45 ignored, 23 SKIPPED (no wave64 etc.). The failure is
execute_indirect_reads_the_arguments_written_before_it, which fails the
same way on main on this GPU. cargo test -p xcl --test e2e: 4 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
